## How Search Works in Newbury

Newbury is the main town in West Berkshire and the home of West Berkshire Council, whose offices are on Market Street. It is a market town, but it also sits on a crossroads: the A34 runs past it north to south, and junction 13 of the M4 at Chieveley is just to the north. That mix shapes who searches for Newbury businesses and how.

Most Newbury firms deal with three kinds of searcher.

**Residents** looking for trades, clinics, solicitors, accountants and shops near home. These searches run through Google's map results, so your Google Business Profile, your reviews and a service page that names Newbury do most of the work.

**Businesses buying from businesses.** Vodafone's head office, Vodafone House, is on The Connection in Newbury, and Greenham Business Park is home to more than 150 businesses. Suppliers to firms like these are judged on detailed service pages and evidence, not on a map listing.

**Visitors.** Newbury Racecourse and the Kennet and Avon Canal, which runs through the town centre, bring people in from outside the district. Pubs, restaurants, hotels and venues need to show up in the searches people make before they travel and on the day.

## What I Do for Newbury Businesses

I offer four kinds of work to Newbury businesses, and most clients start with the audit.

**[Local SEO](/services/local-seo/)**: Google Business Profile categories and services, a steady flow of reviews, consistent name, address and phone details across directories, and pages written for Newbury searches rather than for "Berkshire" in general.

**[Technical SEO audit](/services/technical-seo-audit/)**: a fixed £495 check of crawling, indexing, page speed, mobile layout, structured data and site structure, with a ranked list of fixes you or your developer can act on.

**[Topical authority](/services/topical-authority/) content**: for professional firms and B2B suppliers whose buyers research before they get in touch, I map the questions those buyers ask and build pages that answer them properly.

**[AI search visibility](/services/ai-search-optimisation/)**: I check whether ChatGPT, Google AI Overviews and similar tools mention your business when people ask about your service in West Berkshire, then fix the gaps in what they can find about you.

## Greenham Business Park and B2B Firms

Greenham Business Park sits on the former RAF Greenham Common site. The Greenham Common Trust took the land over from the Ministry of Defence in 1997, and today the park is mostly industrial and mixed-use space.

For firms based there, the map results are rarely the main problem. Their buyers are procurement teams, engineers and operations managers who search for a capability, a standard or a product, often from anywhere in the UK. A single "Services" page does not win those searches.

What usually works better:

- One page per capability, with the specifications, sectors and standards a buyer checks
- Case studies and certifications on the page, where a buyer and Google can both see them
- A site structure that makes the link between your services clear
- Content that answers the questions buyers ask before they shortlist a supplier

I'll help you decide which searches are worth owning and build the pages that can earn them.

## SEO for Thatcham Businesses

Thatcham is a separate town about three miles east of Newbury along the A4. For trades, childcare, clinics and other local services, its closeness to Newbury cuts both ways. Customers will travel between the two, but a Thatcham business can also lose map searches to bigger Newbury competitors.

A Thatcham business usually needs:

- A Google Business Profile with the right service area and categories
- A page that names Thatcham and the nearby areas you cover, rather than relying on a general Newbury page
- Reviews from local customers, asked for in a way that encourages them to mention the job and the town
- Clear opening hours, prices or price ranges, and an easy way to get in touch from a phone

## SEO for Hungerford Businesses

Hungerford is the westernmost of the three towns, served by junction 14 of the M4. Its High Street is known for antiques dealers and independent shops, including the Hungerford Arcade, and it hosts a weekly market on Wednesdays.

Antiques and specialist retail tend to draw buyers from well beyond the town. For a Hungerford shop, that means being found before the trip as well as on the High Street:

- A complete Google Business Profile with accurate opening hours and current photos
- Category or product pages that match what a collector or buyer would type
- Where you sell online, technical foundations that let those pages rank across the UK, not just locally

## How Long SEO Takes in West Berkshire

I won't promise a timeline before I've looked at your site and the businesses you compete with. As a rough guide, fixing your Google Business Profile and technical problems can show changes within a few months, while content-led growth for competitive B2B searches takes longer.

My guide on [how long SEO takes](/blog/how-long-does-seo-take/) explains what affects it.

